# L §4.4, §2.3 (tally 2.3, #247; G3 under the plan's §12a): `one_of` is no form; a row that states it is
# refused at load, `LOAD-PARSE`, with the forms that say it (the stretch `window(d1, dn)`, or one day in a row
# marked `assumed`). Before: `one_of([2026-05-04, 2026-05-11])`.
=== m.tally
model oneof
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input d: date
version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = one_of([2026-05-04, 2026-05-11]) "c"
ask a: d
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: one_of is no form; state the stretch from its first day to its last, window(d1, dn), or one day in a row marked assumed (m.tally:12)
